 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? The quickest way is using an app called Duo Lingo. It sends you pairs of words a week, so you always have fresh learning in each session. Learning a list is faster. Duo Lingo teaches ten words at a time, and you memorize them with a quiz, so you remember the whole lot. Start with something you like, like a short story or a travel blog. You' be surprised how fast you pick up words from context. They' popular for language learning. Another tip, learn word shapes as much as words themselves. Many words sound or look like they do in English, and knowing that helps a lot.",
